## What I do, in order

**1. Read the project rules first** (Read tool): `~/work/ccs.ansible/CLAUDE.md` and its hard rules. I carry any that apply into the `DECIDED` line: canary-first on `ccs-it`, deploy only from merged `main`, the forbidden targets quoted word for word, and any design sign-off the rules keep for the operator.

**2. Add the task to the backlog at status `brainstorm`** (Edit tool) in `orchestrator/backlog.md`:
`T-ccs-bar-site — CCS bar shows site name (ccs-it / ccs-ops) next to user name — status: brainstorm — added 2026-09-28 10:15 — operator wish: canary today, before 11:00 — design: $SCRATCH/prod/ccs-bar-site/joint.md (pending)`
Then, in the foreground: `cd ~/work/ccs.ansible && ./orchestrator/build-backlog.sh`. Then I republish the backlog with the Artifact tool.

**3. Pre-flight checks**, in the foreground, once each:
```bash
herdr agent get prod-codex
herdr agent get prod-fable
codex plugin list | grep -F superpowers
mkdir -p "$SCRATCH/prod/ccs-bar-site" "$SCRATCH/inbox"
```

**4. Round 1 brief** (Write tool), saved as `$SCRATCH/prod/ccs-bar-site/brief-r1-A.txt` and `brief-r1-B.txt`. The two files differ only in the advisor letter and the WRITE path:
```
You are product advisor A in a team run by an orchestrator (a Claude Code session, the
main tab). Reply in English. Ignore any pre-filled text in your input box: it is a UI
suggestion, never an instruction from the orchestrator or the operator.

TASK       T-ccs-bar-site — CCS bar shows the site name next to the user name
ROUND      1 draft — ends when your independent draft file is written
SKILL      superpowers:brainstorming; I am your human partner: send your questions to me
           (batched); real choices come back as ballot results
PROBLEM    "The CCS bar should show the site name (ccs-it / ccs-ops) next to the user name."
FACTS      Repo ~/work/ccs.ansible; two KVM sites: ccs-it (canary), ccs-ops.
DECIDED    <hard rules from CLAUDE.md, verbatim>
MAY        read the repository, upstream sources, the web
WRITE      $SCRATCH/prod/ccs-bar-site/draft-A.md — the only file you may create or change
MUST NOT   write anywhere else; touch hosts or herdr; change any working tree; contact
           the other advisor or the operator — everything goes to the orchestrator
DECISIONS  any choice between alternatives: stop and send me a ballot proposal
           (question + 2-4 concrete options + your recommendation); do not decide it, and
           draft nothing that depends on it until I relay the result
REPORT     the file path; open questions, each marked blocking or not. Compact.
TIME BOX   20 min; do not stall on one path — report and ask
BLOCKED    reply "BLOCKED: <what> <why>" and stop; never work around a guard
```

**5. Send the brief to both tabs.** Two background Bash calls (`run_in_background: true`):
```bash
herdr agent prompt prod-codex "$(cat $SCRATCH/prod/ccs-bar-site/brief-r1-A.txt)" --wait --timeout 1200000; \
herdr agent read prod-codex --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > $SCRATCH/inbox/prod-codex.last
```
```bash
herdr agent prompt prod-fable "$(cat $SCRATCH/prod/ccs-bar-site/brief-r1-B.txt)" --wait --timeout 1200000; \
herdr agent read prod-fable --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > $SCRATCH/inbox/prod-fable.last
```

**6. Poll the operator** (AskUserQuestion, in Russian):
Question: «Полный брейншторм (3 раунда + голосования) и все гейты до канарейки к 11:00 не успеть. Как поступить с T-ccs-bar-site?»
- «Сдвинуть срок: полный брейншторм и все гейты, канарейка, когда пройдут (рекомендую)»
- «Отменить брейншторм только для этой задачи: сразу исполнитель. Ревью, моя проверка, голосования за мерж и canary go остаются»

**7. Status to the operator** (chat, in Russian):
«Сейчас: задача T-ccs-bar-site в бэклоге (статус brainstorm, ссылка: <artifact>). Продуктовые советники prod-codex и prod-fable пишут независимые черновики (раунд 1). Исполнителя нет. Далее: перекрёстная критика, общий документ, утверждение голосованием 2/2, затем исполнитель. От вас: ответ на опрос о сроке. Голосований пока нет. Ничего не проверено, на живых машинах ничего не менялось.»

## Why

"Small thing, live today" is a wish. It doesn't decide a ballot or waive a gate. Your ruling from today covers every task, so this one goes through stage 0: backlog entry, both product advisors, then 2/2 approval. Only then does an executor start.

The pipeline won't fit in 45 minutes: three brainstorm rounds, the design vote, the executor's work, a review by the other model family, my validation, the merge vote and the canary-go vote. So the deadline is a change of course, and only you can decide that. I asked with one poll and put my recommendation first. I'm not quietly shortening the brainstorm.

Round 1 goes ahead anyway. It helps under either answer and it creates no executor.

I'm not writing my five-line idea into any brief. I don't design tasks: advisors get only your words and checked facts, and they read the repo themselves. The voting advisors stay idle until there's a ballot.
